// Test: bugfixes/codegen_f64_bridge_return_coercion
// Regression: CODEGEN_F64 fingerprint 1a20405b — RETURN side coercion missing.
//
// The first fix (f7be2ca) only inserted F64ConvertI32S on the parameter side
// (i32 arg → Number param). The reported follow-up showed the mismatch was
// actually on the RETURN side: a bridge function returning one type was being
// stored into a local of a different MIR type, with no coercion emitted.
//
// In the call-destination path, the codegen consults `function_signatures` and
// then `function_return_types` for the source type. For bridge wrappers that
// are not registered in either (plugin-DSL-generated helpers, HTTP server
// wrappers, etc.), both lookups returned None and `store_to_local` ran without
// a source type — skipping the i32↔f64 conversion entirely.
//
// The fix adds a final lookup against the wasm_generator's
// `wasm_function_return_types` registry (populated by every `register_function`
// / `register_import_function`), so the WASM-emitted return type is always
// available as the source for coercion.
//
// This test stores the result of an i32-returning frame.ui bridge function
// into a `number` (f64) local. Without the fix this emits invalid WASM with
// "type mismatch: expected f64, found i32" at local.set. With the fix the
// codegen emits F64ConvertI32S after the call.

plugins:
	frame.ui

start:
	number observerId = _ui_observe_visible(".target", "visible")
	print(observerId.toString())
